  "headline": "CBA's Group net interest margin increased 9 basis points to 208 bps in FY25 (from 199 bps in FY24). The improvement was primarily driven by a 7 bps benefit from reduced liquid assets and pooled facilities, and a 9 bps positive contribution from capital and replicating portfolio earnings. These were partially offset by a 7 bps headwind from higher funding costs due to deposit price competition and a 1 bps negative impact from basis risk. Asset pricing and portfolio mix were flat.",
